{
  "@context": {
    "schema": "https://schema.org/"
  },
  "@type": "Note",
  "@id": "note:notion-271",
  "title": "GOSSIP",
  "author": "person:jane-brew:001",
  "status": "draft",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "GOSSIP"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "What You're Building"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-7",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A **web app** (likely browser-based or thin client)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A **Rust-based P2P node** running iroh/sendme for inter-peer communication."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-5",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "These nodes need to run **per user, per org, or per device**."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-6",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Rust node should **run in the background**, communicate with the front-end, and be orchestrated gracefully."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Architectural Blueprint"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Here are the core decisions you’ll face, mapped to viable approaches:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-12",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. **Deployment Model: Where does the Rust process run?**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-13",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Option A: **Local Node per User (Electron, Tauri, or Native App)**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-19",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-14",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Rust runs locally on the user's machine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-15",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Your app is a desktop client (e.g., Tauri-based)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-16",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Communication is direct (Rust ↔ frontend)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-17",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Best for:** Full decentralization, offline-first design."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-18",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Tradeoff:** Requires app installation, not pure web."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-20",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Option B: **Rust Service in Backend (Centralized Relay Model)**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-26",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-21",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Rust runs as a background service on your infrastructure."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-22",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Web app communicates with this service."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-23",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Each org/user may have a persistent gossip node."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-24",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Best for:** Server-mediated hybrid P2P (like Matrix or ActivityPub)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-25",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Tradeoff:** Not fully peer-to-peer; more centralized overhead."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-27",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Option C: **Browser-integrated via WebAssembly (Experimental)**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-32",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-28",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Compile Rust to WebAssembly and run it in the browser."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-29",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "May hit WASI or networking constraints (P2P in browser is hard)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-30",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Best for:** Prototyping lightweight, browser-native solutions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-31",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Tradeoff:** Sendme may not yet support Wasm/browser natively."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-33",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-34",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. **Communication between Web App and Rust**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-35",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Depending on the deployment model:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-37",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-36",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**If running locally (Tauri/Electron):**"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-38",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Use `window.__TAURI__.invoke()` to call Rust functions."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-39",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Web frontend is a thin UI layer; Rust handles networking and gossip."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-41",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-40",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**If running server-side:**"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-42",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Use HTTP/WebSocket for frontend ↔ Rust service."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-43",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Each org/workspace has a persistent \"gossip pod\" in your backend infra."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-45",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-44",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**If running as a CLI launched from web (e.g., via server or job runner):**"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-46",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Spawn Rust process from your backend (Node.js, Go, etc.)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-47",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Use IPC, files, or ports for interaction."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-48",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-49",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Gossip Use Cases (Clarifying Purpose)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-50",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "It’s worth pinning down what the gossip system enables:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-55",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-51",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Presence / Awareness:** Who’s online in a workspace?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-52",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Data Sharing:** Sending/receiving blobs, configs, or updates?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-53",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Synchronization:** Conflict resolution? State propagation?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-54",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Privacy Model:** End-to-end encryption? Trust boundaries?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-56",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Your answer here determines **how tightly coupled** this gossip node needs to be to the user’s session and identity."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-57",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-58",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Suggested Next Step"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-59",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Let’s clarify:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-60",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. Do we expect **each user** to run a Rust gossip node, or is it **one per workspace/server**?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-61",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. Does our app **require decentralization**, or is server coordination acceptable?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-62",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. Are we open to hybrid models (e.g., server hosts nodes, browser is client)?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-63",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Once that’s clear, I can design the runtime orchestration—whether spawning background services, integrating via WebSocket, or exploring browser-native P2P possibilities."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}